.SH DESCRIPTION
The QServerSocket class provides a TCP-based server.
.PP
This class is not yet documented.
.PP
See also: QSocket, QSocketDevice, QSocketAddress and QSocketNotifier.
.SH MEMBER FUNCTION DOCUMENTATION
.SH "QServerSocket::QServerSocket ( QObject * parent=0, const char * name=0 )"
Creates a server socket object, but does not start any server yet.
.PP
The \fIparent\fR and \fIname\fR arguments are passed on as usual to the QObject constructor.
.SH "QServerSocket::QServerSocket ( int port, QObject * parent=0, const char * name=0 )"
Creates a server socket object, ands starts a server on the given \fIport.\fR
.PP
The \fIparent\fR and \fIname\fR arguments are passed on as usual to the QObject constructor.
.SH "QServerSocket::~QServerSocket ()"
Destructs the socket.
.SH "QSocketDevice * QServerSocket::socketDevice () \fC[protected]\fR"
Returns the QSocketDevice used by this server.
